WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:09.050
Ultimately, when it is all said and done,
it will not be what you own or how much money

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.550
you are worth that matters.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:17.070
What will truly matter is what you have done
to earn what you own.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:22.910
The lines often blur between what we have
done and what we own because what we own is

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:30.080
a tangible way to distinguish and believe
that what we have done has value.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:36.999
If I do something and receive a certain amount
of money for it, then it is fair to assume

00:00:36.999 --> 00:00:42.969
that what I did had value equal to the money
I received for it.

00:00:42.969 --> 00:00:48.309
But this method of determining real value
in life is not always accurate.

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:55.949
Although it may be true that what I did had
monetary value, it is not necessarily true

00:00:55.949 --> 00:01:00.000
that what I did had any personal value.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.890
And it is just as important, if not more so,
to have personal interest in the things we

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:12.190
do in order to claim any real value in them.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:19.290
It is very possible to own lots of things
and have lots of money but still do very little

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:24.840
in terms of creating pride, value, and contribution
in life.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:31.290
And that is a very important distinction we
must make.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:39.710
We live in a time where there is massive opportunity
to find creative value, interest, and fulfillment

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:42.480
in what we do for work.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:49.630
Simultaneously, we also live in a time where
making money in meaningless roundabout ways

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:52.210
is easier than ever.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:57.750
People are selling eBooks on how to write
and sell eBooks.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:03.590
People are selling webinars on how to make
and sell webinars.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:09.920
People are making YouTube channels, not for
the love of video creation, but for the sole

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:16.920
purpose of making money at any cost of quality
and authenticity.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:22.690
This is not to single out those who participate
in any of these areas.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:29.370
There are, and have previously been, endless
ways in which people make money only for the

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:38.090
sake of making money, void of personal interest
or fulfillment in what they do.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:43.450
Anyone who works for a company that they do
not care about in a position that they do

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.720
not like.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:52.080
And anyone who chooses to do things or follow
career paths that sacrifice their values,

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:58.940
interests, and passions solely out of the
desire and desperation for wealth are all

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:07.280
examples of feeble self-sacrifice
Surely life requires sacrifice, but when it

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:12.640
comes to making money, what is the right amount
of sacrifice?

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:16.200
Is it more important to make larger sums of
money?

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:23.140
Or is it more important to maintain integrity
and authenticity?

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:29.209
It is clear that there must be a balance,
but when we determine this balance for our

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:38.230
self, we must remember that what matters most
in life is what we do, not what we own.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:44.540
The only things that will make us truly feel
alive are our experiences.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:48.910
How honest we can remain to our self and those
we care about.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:55.740
And how much we can contribute to what we
believe in and enjoy.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:04:01.849
Of course we need to make money in order to
do these things, but we must ask ourselves

00:04:01.849 --> 00:04:09.120
how much money is enough money, and how much
self is enough self?

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:15.310
Whatever balance it takes to ensure that you
will be able to look back and appreciate the

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:21.489
depth of your connection to life and know
that you never shortchanged yourself, is the

00:04:21.489 --> 00:04:50.720
balance you must create.

